<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00754</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</md:title>
    <md:uuid>486fae87-6225-4c5a-927a-076f5e4b30ea</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">A.
            <media alt="Scatter plot showing cost in dollars versus distance in miles. The data points form a roughly straight line, indicating cost increases with distance from 0 to 10 miles and $0 to $22.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_01.svg"/>
            </media>
            </para>
          <para id="para-00003">B.
            <media alt="A scatter plot showing points representing weight (milligrams) on the y-axis and height (millimeters) on the x-axis, with values ranging from 0–22 for weight and 0–10 for height.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_02.svg"/>
            </media>
            </para>
          <para id="para-00004">C.
            <media alt="Scatter plot showing a negative correlation between precipitation (cm) on the x-axis and water used for irrigation (thousands of gallons) on the y-axis; as precipitation increases, irrigation water use decreases.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_03.svg"/>
            </media>
            </para>
          <para id="para-00005">D.<media alt="Scatter plot showing number of phytoplankton (in tens of thousands) increasing sharply as temperature rises from 0°C to 10°C, with a noticeable spike above 6°C.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_04.svg"/>
            </media>
            </para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00007">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">A doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that fit a line well
            and are increasing.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">B doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a
            line well and do not show a pattern.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">C doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would fit a line
            well and are decreasing.</para>
          <para id="para-00011">D doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a
            line well and do show a curved pattern.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
